written to during install  MakeFileSystemRw only works on filesystems which can be made writable, but doesn't check ensure that the filesystem is writable at all. This change checks that if the filesystem has the squashfs id at the beginning, and if so, does not modify it at all.  Also, it removes the unused &quot;rw&quot; argument from &quot;MakeFileSystemRw&quot; Given its name, it should always make the filesystem rw, and is currently always used that way.  BUG=chromium:666530  TEST=I did good things.  Change-Id: I2fc0b8304468aab2757593a56f50e1f0a41fe3b1 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/412271 Commit-Ready: Matthew Mirman &lt;mirman@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Matthew Mirman &lt;mirman@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Andrew de los Reyes &lt;adlr@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="412271" owner_email="mirman@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/71/412271/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2493975c774bdb009eb1404f5aa8e77753579072" commit="76eea043e25b6c7a7d37bf0efa5c093a2b0be555" commit_message="Update Noto Color Emoji to the latest  NotoColorEmoji.ttf is updated to the latest release (as included in the latest Android OS release). It supports Unicode Emoji version 4. ( http://unicode.org/emoji/charts/emoji-released.html  and   http://unicode.org/emoji/charts/full-emoji-list.html )    In addition, Noto*Lao* fonts are updated with a minor fix.  ( https://github.com/googlei18n/noto-fonts/issues/715 : shouldn't affect CrOS).   BUG=None TEST=At the first URL above, the browser column is rendered identically to the Google column.  Change-Id: I2493975c774bdb009eb1404f5aa8e77753579072 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/414249 Commit-Ready: Jungshik Shin &lt;jshin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Jungshik Shin &lt;jshin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="414249" owner_email="jshin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/49/414249/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I135eba783982401822f077668c34bd9ef96eac39" commit="9283dcb7560a3667f72289410a9d1a625075172d" commit_message="Add static configurations to the Google Router.  Add static configurations to the Google router in Chaos Lab.  BUG=669697 TEST=None  Change-Id: I135eba783982401822f077668c34bd9ef96eac39 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/414534 Commit-Ready: Ashakiran Byrappa &lt;abyrappa@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Ashakiran Byrappa &lt;abyrappa@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Tien Chang &lt;tienchang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="414534" owner_email="abyrappa@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/34/414534/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Iabbdfa1dfa574d4f48631f182e198c520e671b2b" commit="90a9c510546c431bdf212f7c23e6f715ed39c60a" commit_message="CHROMIUM: arm64: dts: mt8173-hana: increase i2c0 clk to 200 kHz  Increase the clk of I2C0 to 200 kHz in order to follow the timing contraint of I2C spec in fast mode.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:59942 TEST=pass I2C0 system integrity test @ 200 kHz  Change-Id: Iabbdfa1dfa574d4f48631f182e198c520e671b2b Signed-off-by: Milton Chiang &lt;milton.chiang@mediatek.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/414768 Reviewed-by: Philip Chen &lt;philipchen@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="414768" owner_email="milton.chiang@mediatek.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/68/414768/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic2a1b5b40cec382098058fdd75c9954d84c74e03" commit="8dbd392e70422384646e5c063225c90dc8c096a9" commit_message="hostapd: Stop EAPOL exchange when station is disconnected  If AP-STA four-way handshake is in progress and at the same time if disconnection triggered or AP-STA disconnection is in progress and GTK renewal happens, AP might still proceed four-way handshake/GTK renewal which would lead in unnecessary retry of eapol frames and thus ending up in false failure. To fix the bug, check association flag before sending four-way handshake/GTK frames.  BUG=b:32360260 TEST=tested by transitioning station from 2.4G to 5G.  Change-Id: Ic2a1b5b40cec382098058fdd75c9954d84c74e03 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/402469 Commit-Ready: NARAYANRADDI MASTI &lt;nmasti@google.com&gt; Tested-by: NARAYANRADDI MASTI &lt;nmasti@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Zhihong Yu &lt;zhihongyu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="402469" owner_email="nmasti@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/third_party/hostap" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/hostap" ref="refs/changes/69/402469/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="Ic2da9138f78e4b226d61bf3d29c0733e4af78d8a" commit="b692ca1ff3208f89c169a5c1b451401525f0c61b" commit_message="CHROMIUM: iio: cros_ec: Enable EC fifo int when buffer is used.  Instead of enabling the FIFO interrupt when cros_ec_ring is loaded, enable it only when the buffer is used. Otherwise, if the FIFO is full but the buffer is not used, the EC will send an avalanche of interrupts.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:55849 TEST=Check that until ARC++ is launched there are not interrupt coming from the EC. Once ARC++ is running the interrupts are allowed. Used &quot; ectool motionsense fifo_int_enable&quot;. Check that if we enable a sensor but not the buffer, no interrupts are generated.  Change-Id: Ic2da9138f78e4b226d61bf3d29c0733e4af78d8a Signed-off-by: Gwendal Grignou &lt;gwendal@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/412450 Reviewed-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="412450" owner_email="gwendal@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/50/412450/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I0de70ec798b8da77da1d53b0297fe217ee935155" commit="afa9b2038ef81d8797d5526312719d08d49d6c5e" commit_message="trunks: add 'open' to seccomp filters  When an error is detected in TpmUtility::CheckState(), trunksd crashes when minijail blocks 'open' syscall. Can be seen on the simulator, where there is no firmware to initialize the TPM.  BUG=chromium:669109 TEST=Start on the simulator, no &quot;blocked syscall: open&quot; in logs.  Change-Id: I0de70ec798b8da77da1d53b0297fe217ee935155 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/414952 Commit-Ready: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Darren Krahn &lt;dkrahn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="414952" owner_email="apronin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="aosp/platform/system/tpm" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/aosp/platform/system/tpm" ref="refs/changes/52/414952/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I906722addf1804d83990c1b91cb1cb04d1619be8" commit="199cb7f16182e1e8b3a40185e684e78888454c1e" commit_message="drivers/b